<h2 id="outlook">The Jets' Backfield Without Him</h2>
<p>With Hall out, Braelon Allen and Isaiah Davis are expected to carry the load. Allen was limited to four games last season by a knee injury but flashed in the preseason with a 31-yard touchdown run, while Davis missed much of training camp with a knee issue of his own. Neither is expected to replicate Hall's explosiveness, which matters for a Jets offense already dealing with a long list of injuries, including at left guard, tight end and receiver.</p>
<div class="callout">
<strong>Reading the Injury</strong>
  A quad strain is a soft-tissue injury, not a verdict on Hall's athletic ceiling, and the early MRI news was good. It is still the second lower-body issue of his season after the August groin strain, and for a back whose value is built on explosive acceleration, how he looks in his first games back will say more than any combine number.
</div>
